    S = A.post[pv]
    # feasible types
    gastables = ... (for transfer/deposit)
    # key for garantía ops: choose from keys with activo>0 for retiro, vencido>0 for liberacion
    ops = Tuple{Symbol, ...}[]
    if !isempty(gastables): push transfer, deposit
    # withdrawal keys
    claves_retiro = [k for (k,g) in S.garantias if g.activo>0 && isempty(g.en_retirada)]
    # liberation keys: vencido computed at slot
    claves_lib = [...]
    # weights
    ...
    pick one op with weighted random among feasible
    build tx with nonce = nonce_de(S, clave) (+ error with prob 0.10)
end
```

Wait: "nonce = nonce_de(S, clave); con probabilidad 0,10, un nonce erróneo (n + 1, o n − 1 si n > 0, al 50 %)". Note: for a deposit to a key, the clave is o.dueño; nonce_de(S, o.dueño). For withdraw/liberation, clave = chosen key.

Also note: The "wrong nonce" is n+1, or n−1 if n>0, at 50%. So `if n>0 && rand(rng)<0.5: n-1 else n+1`. Actually "n − 1 si n > 0, al 50 %" means: with the 0.10 probability, choose between n+1 and (n−1 if n>0) each 50%. If n==0, always n+1. Implement:
```
function nonce_con_error(rng, n)
    if rand(rng) < 0.10
        if n > 0 && rand(rng) < 0.5
            return n - UInt64(1)
        else
            return n + UInt64(1)
        end
    end
    return n
end
```

But careful: the wrong nonce should be generated for the operation, but the operation is built against `S`, and the nonce check uses the state at application. If n=0 and n+1=1, likely ErrNonce. Good.

