So remove the duplicate "generadas" vs "construidas" and use one `construidas` = generated. Then the ErrNonce percentage = ErrNonce / construidas(garantía) = ~15-20%. 

But wait — is that the intended anti-gaming? If someone constructs tons of ops in non-selected branches with correct nonce, they'd dilute the percentage. But the generator builds against valid states and only one op per block; the non-selected branches are a legitimate part of the DAG. I think the literal reading is best. Let me go with `construidas` = all generated ops. I'll still report `evaluadas = aplicadas + descartadas` and `no_seleccionadas = construidas - evaluadas`.

